    <h1 class="rv in" style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem);max-width:20ch">Is a 2 Hour Boat Trip Enough in Madeira, or Should You Book 3 Hours?</h1>
    <div class="artmeta rv in d1"><span>1 December 2026</span><span>5 min read</span><span>Funchal · Madeira</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="pad">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="article rv">
      <p class="lede">Two hours is enough for a sunset run from Funchal to Cabo Girão and back, but not for swimming. The shortest trip with swim stops is the 2h30 Day Trip, and the 3 hour version adds 30 minutes further west to Ponta do Sol.</p>

      <h2>What do 2 hours, 2h30 and 3 hours actually buy you?</h2><p>Distance along the coast, mostly. Everything on a Chifbay trip happens west of Funchal, on the south coast, and each extra half hour pushes the turning point further along it. Measured in a straight line from Marina do Funchal, Câmara de Lobos is about 6 km away, Cabo Girão about 9 km, Fajã dos Padres about 10 km, Ribeira Brava about 15 km and Ponta do Sol a little under 19 km. The boat follows the shore, so the real distance is a bit more.</p><p>Here is what each length looks like on the water.</p><h3>Sunset Trip, 2 hours: 400 EUR</h3><ul><li>Casts off 1 h 15 before sunset, which means near 16:45 in December and near 20:00 in June.</li><li>Runs west past the Funchal seafront and Câmara de Lobos.</li><li>Turns under Cabo Girão, the 580 metre cliff, as the light goes gold.</li><li>Comes home with the sun down, back about 45 minutes after sunset, with Funchal's lights coming on.</li><li>No swimming.</li></ul><h3>Sunset Trip, 2h30: 500 EUR</h3><ul><li>Same start, same light.</li><li>Carries on past Cabo Girão and Fajã dos Padres and turns at Ribeira Brava.</li><li>Back about 1 hour 15 minutes after sunset, well into the dark.</li><li>No swimming.</li></ul><h3>Day Trip, 2h30: 500 EUR</h3><ul><li>Leaves at 10:00 or 14:00, back at 12:30 or 16:30.</li><li>Câmara de Lobos, then Cabo Girão, with drone shots from above when the weather allows.</li><li>Fajã dos Padres: swim, jump in, paddle boards.</li><li>Ribeira Brava: a second swim.</li><li>A fast run back to Funchal.</li></ul><h3>Day Trip, 3 hours: 600 EUR</h3><ul><li>Leaves at 10:00 or 14:00, back at 13:00 or 17:00.</li><li>Everything on the 2h30 route.</li><li>Then an extra half hour west, as far as Ponta do Sol, a village with its church and seafront tucked under a cliff.</li></ul><h2>Is 2 hours enough?</h2><p>For a sunset, yes. Two hours from Funchal is enough to reach Cabo Girão, watch the light change on the cliff and the sea, have a drink and come home under the first lights of the city.</p><p>For swimming, no, because there is no 2 hour Day Trip. The shortest trip with swim stops is the 2h30 Day Trip, and it already includes both swims, at Fajã dos Padres and Ribeira Brava. If being in the water is the point, 2 hours is not an option, and 2h30 is the minimum.</p><h2>What does the extra 30 minutes add on the Sunset Trip?</h2><p>More coast and more dark. Turning at Ribeira Brava rather than Cabo Girão adds about 6 km of coast: past the green ledge of Fajã dos Padres below the cliffs, to where the Ribeira Brava valley meets the sea. You also see the cliff from both sides, once on the way out in daylight and once on the way back in dusk.</p><p>The trade is that the 2h30 trip comes home well after sunset. Some people love the night run back along a lit-up coast. Others prefer to be back on land soon after the colours fade. In winter, when it gets cool after dark, the 2 hour option is often the more comfortable one. Our guide to the <a href="/posts/sunset-cruise-madeira-guide">best light on a sunset cruise in Madeira</a> goes into timing in more detail.</p><h2>Should you book 2h30 or 3 hours for the Day Trip?</h2><p>Book 2h30 if you mainly want the swims and the cliffs. It covers Câmara de Lobos, Cabo Girão, Fajã dos Padres and Ribeira Brava, which is the heart of the route.</p><p>Book 3 hours if you want Ponta do Sol too, or simply more time on the water. Its name means point of the sun, and seeing it from the sea gives you the whole picture of its houses climbing the rock. Our <a href="/posts/ponta-do-sol-madeira-guide">Ponta do Sol guide</a> explains what is there if you want to come back by land later. For 100 EUR more per boat, the extra half hour is good value for a group of four or five, and an easy yes for anyone who does not want the morning to end.</p><h2>Why might the shorter trip be the smarter one?</h2><p>Longer is not always better. We would point you to the shorter option in these cases.</p><ul><li><strong>First time on a small boat.</strong> If someone in the group is not sure how they will feel at sea, 2 hours is a kinder test than 3.</li><li><strong>Anyone prone to seasickness.</strong> Less time at sea means less time to feel it. Read our <a href="/posts/seasickness-boat-trip-madeira-guide">seasickness guide</a> before you choose.</li><li><strong>A tight day.</strong> Cruise passengers on a port day, or anyone with a flight or dinner booking, should keep the margin. A 10:00 trip of 2h30 is back at 12:30.</li><li><strong>Cooler months on the Sunset Trip.</strong> The evening chills quickly after dark, so the 2 hour version often feels just right.</li></ul><h2>Which length should your group book?</h2><ol><li><strong>Do you want to swim?</strong> If yes, it is the Day Trip, so 2h30 or 3 hours. If no, the Sunset Trip, so 2 hours or 2h30.</li><li><strong>Is anyone unsure about boats?</strong> If yes, take the shorter version of whichever trip you chose.</li><li><strong>How full is your day?</strong> With a flight, a ship or a dinner booking to make, keep the shorter option and the margin.</li><li><strong>How many of you are there?</strong> The extra 100 EUR is per boat, so it costs each person less the bigger your group. Shared between five, it is 20 EUR each.</li></ol><h2>Is there a longer trip than 3 hours?</h2><p>No. There is no full-day trip. The two trips are the <a href="/hidden-coves-half-day">Day Trip west to the coves</a>, at 2h30 or 3 hours, and the <a href="/sunset-cruise">Sunset Trip along the cliffs</a>, at 2 hours or 2h30. If you want something at a different time, Chifbay can arrange private custom trips on WhatsApp.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What is the distance to Cabo Girão by sea?</h3><p>Roughly 9 km as the crow flies from the marina, and it is where the 2 hour Sunset Trip turns round.</p><h3>Can you swim on a 2 hour boat trip in Madeira?</h3><p>Not on ours. The 2 hour option is the Sunset Trip, which has no swimming. The shortest trip with swim stops is the 2h30 Day Trip.</p><h3>What does the 3 hour Day Trip add?</h3><p>Thirty minutes further west to Ponta do Sol, on top of Câmara de Lobos, Cabo Girão, Fajã dos Padres and Ribeira Brava.</p><h3>How much more does the longer trip cost?</h3><p>100 EUR more per boat. At sunset you pay 400 EUR for 2h or 500 EUR for 2h30. By day, 2h30 costs 500 EUR and 3h costs 600 EUR.</p>

      <blockquote>Two hours gets you to the cliff and back with the light. Three hours gets you to Ponta do Sol and a slower morning.</blockquote>
    </article>
    <p class="pref-src" data-pref-source><span>Enjoying our Madeira guides?</span> <a href="https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=chifbay.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="#4285F4" d="M23.5 12.3c0-.8-.1-1.6-.2-2.3H12v4.5h6.5a5.6 5.6 0 0 1-2.4 3.6v3h3.9c2.2-2.1 3.5-5.1 3.5-8.8z"/><path fill="#34A853" d="M12 24c3.2 0 6-1.1 7.9-2.9l-3.9-3c-1.1.7-2.4 1.2-4 1.2-3.1 0-5.7-2.1-6.6-4.9h-4v3.1A12 12 0 0 0 12 24z"/><path fill="#FBBC05" d="M5.4 14.4a7.2 7.2 0 0 1 0-4.7V6.6h-4a12 12 0 0 0 0 10.8l4-3z"/><path fill="#EA4335" d="M12 4.8c1.7 0 3.3.6 4.6 1.8l3.4-3.4A12 12 0 0 0 1.4 6.6l4 3.1C6.3 6.9 8.9 4.8 12 4.8z"/></svg>Add Chifbay as a preferred source on Google</a></p>

